---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro'
import BlogPostShell from '../../components/BlogPostShell.astro'
import BlogToolEmbed from '../../components/BlogToolEmbed.astro'

const slug = 'magnetic-field-converter'
const seo = {
  title: 'Tesla to gauss converter — magnetic flux density | maratool',
  description: 'Convert tesla, gauss, millitesla, and gamma — 1 T = 10,000 G exactly. Free browser magnetic field converter.',
  canonical: `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}`,
  schema: {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BlogPosting',
    headline: 'How to convert tesla to gauss',
    image: 'https://maratool.com/og/converter.svg',
    datePublished: '2026-07-25',
    dateModified: '2026-07-25',
    author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Marcell Almeida', url: 'https://marcell.com.br' },
    publisher: {
      '@type': 'Organization',
      name: 'maratool',
      url: 'https://maratool.com',
      logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://maratool.com/favicon.svg' },
    },
    mainEntityOfPage: { '@type': 'WebPage', '@id': `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}` },
    url: `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}`,
    description: 'Convert tesla, gauss, millitesla, and gamma — 1 T = 10,000 G exactly. Free browser magnetic field converter.',
  },
  breadcrumbSchema: {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://maratool.com' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Blog', item: 'https://maratool.com/blog' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'How to convert tesla to gauss', item: `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}` },
    ],
  },
}
---
<Base {...seo}>
  <Layout>
    <BlogPostShell
      title="How to convert tesla to gauss"
      lead="Type a flux density — read tesla, mT, µT, gauss, or gamma instantly."
      date="July 25, 2026"
      dateIso="2026-07-25"
    >
      <p>Magnet datasheets quote gauss in the US and millitesla elsewhere; geophysics logs nanotesla as gamma. The <a href="/magnetic-field-converter/">Tesla to Gauss Converter</a> connects the SI and CGS scales exactly.</p>

      <BlogToolEmbed slug="magnetic-field-converter" title="Try it — convert magnetic flux density units" height={440} />

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Pick units</strong> — "Tesla (T)" to "Gauss (G)", or any other pair.</li>
        <li><strong>Type a value</strong> — the result updates as you type, with swap and copy.</li>
        <li><strong>Copy</strong> — one click, with "Copied!" feedback.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Magnetic flux density conversion factors</h2>
      <p>Every unit converts through the tesla (the base unit). To convert A → B, multiply by A's factor and divide by B's:</p>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Unit</th><th>= this many teslas</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        <tr><td>Tesla (T)</td><td>1</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Millitesla (mT)</td><td>0.001</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Microtesla (µT)</td><td>1.0000 × 10^-6</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Nanotesla (nT)</td><td>1.0000 × 10^-9</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Kilogauss (kG)</td><td>0.1</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Gauss (G)</td><td>0.0001</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Milligauss (mG)</td><td>1.0000 × 10^-7</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Gamma (γ)</td><td>1.0000 × 10^-9</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>When you need it</h2>
      <p>Anchors: Earth’s field ≈ 50 µT (0.5 G), a neodymium magnet surface ≈ 0.3–0.5 T (3,000–5,000 G), MRI machines 1.5–3 T, and magnetometer surveys resolve single gammas (nT).</p>

      <h2>Sources & methodology</h2>
      <p>Conversion factors follow <a href="https://www.nist.gov/pml/special-publication-811" rel="noopener" target="_blank">NIST Special Publication 811</a>; exact-by-definition factors are marked in the tool itself. All math runs client-side in your browser — nothing is uploaded.</p>

      <h2>More conversion guides</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/blog/magnetic-field-strength-converter/">How to convert oersted to A/m (magnetic field strength)</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/magnetic-flux-converter/">How to convert weber to maxwell (magnetic flux)</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/inductance-converter/">How to convert henries, mH, and µH inductor values</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p>Or browse everything at once in the <a href="/blog/new-unit-converters/">new unit &amp; sizing converters roundup</a>.</p>

      <hr class="blog-divider" />
      <p class="blog-footer-note">The <a href="/magnetic-field-converter/">Tesla to Gauss</a> tool is free, runs locally, and never sends your data to a server. More <a href="/converter/">converter tools</a> at <a href="/">maratool.com</a>.</p>
    </BlogPostShell>
  </Layout>
</Base>
